<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's AAPT plans big telephone price cuts.</title>
<headline>Australia's AAPT plans big telephone price cuts.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>AAPT Telecommunications Pty Ltd said on Monday it plans to cut the price of its long distance telephone services by up to 60 percent from Tuesday, the start of deregulation in Australia's telecommunications industry.</p>
<p>AAPT chief executive officer Larry Williams said he hopes to snarl between eight and 10 percent of the long distance market, which would mainly be at the expense of Telstra Corp Ltd and Optus Communications Pty Ltd.</p>
<p>Williams said he expected AAPT to get its official 'carrier' licence from the government, making it Australia's third official carrier after Telstra and Optus.</p>
</text>
